# 5. Component Description

## Arduino UNO

Arduino UNO acts as the central controller of the system. It reads sensor values and executes the irrigation control algorithm.

## DHT11 Sensor

Measures:

* Temperature (°C)
* Humidity (%)

The sensor communicates digitally with the Arduino.

## Soil Moisture Sensor

Measures moisture content present in the soil.

The sensor provides analog output which is converted into moisture percentage.

## LDR Sensor

Measures light intensity.

Resistance decreases when light intensity increases.

## Relay Module

Acts as an electrical switch between Arduino and solenoid valve.

## Solenoid Valve

Controls water flow to plants.

The valve opens when the relay is energized.

