# 9. Calibration Methodology

## Soil Moisture Sensor Calibration

The sensor was tested under different soil conditions.

### Dry Soil

Sensor inserted in dry soil.

Observed reading:

* Approximately 300

### Wet Soil

Sensor inserted in wet soil.

Observed reading:

* Approximately 800

### Threshold Selection

Midpoint selected:

* Threshold = 500

Decision:

* Below threshold → Irrigation ON
* Above threshold → Irrigation OFF

---

## DHT11 Calibration

The DHT11 readings were compared with ambient room conditions.

Measured values remained within expected range.

Typical values observed:

* Temperature: 25°C – 32°C
* Humidity: 50% – 80%

---

## LDR Calibration

Measurements recorded under:

### Bright Sunlight

High analog readings.

### Indoor Lighting

Moderate readings.

### Dark Environment

Low readings.

Threshold adjusted experimentally.

---

# 10. Control Logic

The following logic was implemented:

IF soil moisture is below threshold:

* Turn relay ON
* Open solenoid valve
* Start irrigation

ELSE

* Turn relay OFF
* Close solenoid valve

This process repeats continuously.

